  "id": "EUVD-2026-128507",
  "enisaUuid": "ad8499e8-7f82-3556-bd7a-241f93ec0b74",
  "description": "In Eclipse versions 1.5-1.6.13, 2.0.0-2.0.22 and 2.1.0-2.1.2, the client library libmosquitto does not reject Will messages with payloads greater than 65535 bytes when calling `mosquitto_will_set()` or `mosquitto_will_set_v5()`. This results in up to 65535 bytes of uninitialised heap memory being transmitted as the Will.\n\n\n\nThis can be mitigated by only passing payloads with a maximum length of 65535 bytes.",
